{'symbol': 'XOM', 'date': '2020-05-01 10:30:00', 'title': 'EXXONMOBIL REPORTS Q1 LOSS OF $0.14 PER SHARE', 'text': "REPORTS RESULTS FOR FIRST QUARTER 2020.Q1 LOSS PER SHARE $0.14.SAYS REDUCING 2020 CAPITAL AND OPERATING SPEND TO MANAGE UNPRECEDENTED MARKET CHALLENGES.Q1 LOSS OF $610 MILLION DRIVEN BY $2.9 BILLION NONCASH CHARGE FROM MARKET-RELATED WRITE-DOWNS.QUARTERLY OIL‑EQUIVALENT PRODUCTION WAS 4 MILLION BARRELS PER DAY, UP 2 PERCENT FROM Q1 OF 2019.SAYS CAPEX IS NOW EXPECTED TO BE APPROXIMATELY $23 BILLION FOR YEAR, DOWN FROM PREVIOUSLY ANNOUNCED GUIDANCE OF $33 BILLION..SAYS EXCLUDING ENTITLEMENT EFFECTS AND DIVESTMENTS, QUARTERLY OIL‑EQUIVALENT PRODUCTION WAS UP 5 PERCENT FROM PRIOR YEAR.QUARTERLY LOSS $610 MILLION VERSUS. $2.35 BILLION EARNINGS REPORTED LAST YEAR.SAYS REDUCING 2020 CAPITAL SPENDING BY 30 PERCENT AND CASH OPERATING EXPENSES BY 15 PERCENT.QUARTERLY CAPITAL AND EXPLORATION EXPENDITURES WERE $7.14 BILLION VERSUS $6.89 BILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.SAYS COVID-19 HAS SIGNIFICANTLY IMPACTED NEAR-TERM DEMAND, RESULTING IN OVERSUPPLIED MARKETS, UNPRECEDENTED PRESSURE ON COMMODITY PRICES, MARGINS.SAYS EXXONMOBIL'S CAPITAL ALLOCATION PRIORITIES REMAIN UNCHANGED.QUARTERLY UPSTREAM EARNINGS WERE $536 MILLION VERSUS $2.88 BILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.QUARTERLY RESULTS INCLUDED A $2.9 BILLION CHARGE FROM IDENTIFIED ITEMS, OR $0.67 PER SHARE ASSUMING DILUTION.QUARTERLY WORLDWIDE REFINERY THROUGHPUT 4,060 KBD VERSUS. 3,886 KBD REPORTED LAST YEAR."}{'symbol': 'XOM', 'date': '2020-05-01 06:30:00', 'title': 'OIL SEARCH TO UNDERTAKE FURTHER MEASURES TO REDUCE BREAKEVEN COSTS', 'text': 'PLAN TO UNDERTAKE FURTHER MEASURES TO REDUCE BREAKEVEN COSTS ACROSS BUSINESS AND TO OPTIMISE CAPITAL MANAGEMENT.NOW IN MORE ROBUST POSITION AND ABLE TO WITHSTAND SUSTAINED PERIOD OF LOW OIL PRICES AND MARKET VOLATILITY.SINCE JAN, PLAYED ROLE IN FACILITATING INFORMAL DISCUSSIONS BETWEEN EXXONMOBIL & PNG GOVERNMENT TO HELP BRIDGE GAP ON P\'NYANG GAS AGREEMENT.HAD NO DISRUPTIONS TO OPERAT